{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see","id":990848,"title":"What Mantles would you like to see?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-21T01:13:46-07:00","id":990848,"title":"What Mantles would you like to see?","content":"So the stretch goal to add a section exploring the Mantles of various gods in the Companion as divine parents, patrons, and creators. With twelve and a half Pantheons on the table just in Hero and the Companion, we're certainly not hurting for options, so I was curious to see which specific gods and Mantles of those gods you'd like to see covered in the section.<br /> <br /> The obvious one that jumps out at me is the pretty severe gulf of character between the Greek Ares and the Roman Mars, to the point that they scarcely read as the same god (the former a bloody brute largely scorned, the latter a noble conqueror and patron of the empire), and I'm really excited to see how wildly different those aspects and the Scions created by each one appear. I'm also wondering if the Quetzalcoatl/Kukulkan divide (as well as other 'shared' gods) can be addressed even though we aren't seeing the Mayan Pantheon until Demigod, especially seeing how much more bloody and horrifying the Teotl seem than their predecessors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T01:24:20-07:00","id":990852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see#post990848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the stretch goal to add a section exploring the Mantles of various gods in the Companion as divine parents, patrons, and creators. With twelve and a half Pantheons on the table just in Hero and the Companion, we're certainly not hurting for options, so I was curious to see which specific gods and Mantles of those gods you'd like to see covered in the section.<br /> <br /> The obvious one that jumps out at me is the pretty severe gulf of character between the Greek Ares and the Roman Mars, to the point that they scarcely read as the same god (the former a bloody brute largely scorned, the latter a noble conqueror and patron of the empire), and I'm really excited to see how wildly different those aspects and the Scions created by each one appear. I'm also wondering if the Quetzalcoatl/Kukulkan divide (as well as other 'shared' gods) can be addressed even though we aren't seeing the Mayan Pantheon until Demigod, especially seeing how much more bloody and horrifying the Teotl seem than their predecessors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not technically a mantle, but I'd like it if some discussion involving Freya, Sekhmet, and Ixchel were brought up, as they all represent similar purviews and personality traits across immense geographical distances. <br /> <br /> As for mantles, I'm transgender, so I'm a little bit biased? I'd love to see something of a Venus Castina mantle for Aprhodite, something touching on Odin's multiple paths to magic, including his time studying under Freya. This is a sensitive subject because historical accuracy is very important to the Scion community, and there are plenty of people who feel such things would only be 'politically correct for the sake of politically correct', but the culture of humanity is far more complex now than ever it was before, and it would be nice to see some modernization mantles, things that reflect how a god or goddess has grown in the past millennia and how they view modern culture/social issues. A mantle of Thor trying to get his hammer back might be sympathetic toward transmen, or the like. A mantle for Persephone as Queen of the Underworld would be great, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T01:27:18-07:00","id":990854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=990852#post990852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not technically a mantle, but I'd like it if some discussion involving Freya, Sekhmet, and Ixchel were brought up, as they all represent similar purviews and personality traits across immense geographical distances.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd mentioned the Sekhmet-Ixchel connection elsewhere and it's honestly one of the most novel mythological ideas I've ever heard. Plus, it ties into the conspiracy theories about the Egyptians crossing the Atlantic!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for mantles, I'm transgender, so I'm a little bit biased? I'd love to see something of a Venus Castina mantle for Aprhodite, something touching on Odin's multiple paths to magic, including his time studying under Freya. This is a sensitive subject because historical accuracy is very important to the Scion community, and there are plenty of people who feel such things would only be 'politically correct for the sake of politically correct', but the culture of humanity is far more complex now than ever it was before, and it would be nice to see some modernization mantles, things that reflect how a god or goddess has grown in the past millennia and how they view modern culture/social issues. A mantle of Thor trying to get his hammer back might be sympathetic toward transmen, or the like. A mantle for Persephone as Queen of the Underworld would be great, too. </div> </div> </div>My own bias wants me to see Osiris as a transwoman, but I'd much rather play that as an Incarnate Scion than have that be a Mantle tucked away in some supplement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T03:44:36-07:00","id":990886,"title":"","content":"Sorry guys, but i didn't understand well what mantle is:<br /> <br /> The &quot;mantle&quot; a god can wear is the other face of the god? maybe in another culture? <br /> <br /> For example: Mithra is a god in Yazata Pantheon, in Deva And he's loved even by Roman. All this face of the same god are different mantle? <br /> <br /> Hades - Pluto <br /> Venus - Aphrodite<br /> <br /> When a god is shared between pantheons, he's changing the mantle...? right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T03:53:24-07:00","id":990889,"title":"","content":"Something like that.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm greedy - I want all the mantles. I kind of halfway suspect this is how we'll get Hathor and Sekhmet into the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T05:47:08-07:00","id":990918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=990886#post990886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry guys, but i didn't understand well what mantle is:<br /> <br /> The &quot;mantle&quot; a god can wear is the other face of the god? maybe in another culture?<br /> <br /> For example: Mithra is a god in Yazata Pantheon, in Deva And he's loved even by Roman. All this face of the same god are different mantle?<br /> <br /> Hades - Pluto<br /> Venus - Aphrodite<br /> <br /> When a god is shared between pantheons, he's changing the mantle...? right?</div> </div> </div> </div>A mantle can be a bit tricky to nail down, because different cultures seem to 'do it' differently. As an example, there could be a version of Odin who is a nameless wanderer, and a version of Odin who is King of the Gods. If you've ever read the novel American Gods (and if you haven't I highly recommend it, though I prefer the short stories set in it a lot more) then that's a very good example. Mr. Wednesday is much more an American Businessman and King/CEO of the gods, another version of him comes up who emphasizes his traits differently. Greece Ares is kind of the worst things about innocence, in Astrology Ares is the first Scion, and represents humanity at its most childlike, prone to throwing tantrums, and used to getting whatever it wants from the world and people around it without considering the situation of anyone but itself. In Astrology, Ares only avoids being a purely negative sign in that it can be tempered into a disciplined adult with time; ironically this is mirrored in the relationship between Ares and Mars. Ares in Greek mythology is not positive, often loses control and creates great battles that humanity and gods are better off not taking part in, and in general is depicted fairly childishly. In Rome, the god Mars is almost entirely a different person, representing cold calculated disciplined warfare and the tactics used to break less structured combatants, it also has the 'Gates of Mars' and other such things of interest.<br /> <br /> When I run my games, I tend to make the Aztec Pantheon less a distinct entity and more as a different mantle for each of the Mayan gods, 'Reversed' (in a taort-esque sense). I do this because many of the Aztec gods have titles like: Our Lord the Flayed One, or Tezcatlipoca: We Are His Slaves. Coyolxauhqui, whose severed head constituted the moon because apparently a mother seeing her daughter's severed head each night is comforting. If you look at almost any Aztec god, they have much in common with their Mayan/Olmec counterparts, but they'll almost always be just a little bit 'darker', which in my 1st edition games I would qualify as the old Pantheon taking extreme steps to save a civilization choked by climate change and improper management of resources, whatever magic they used led them down a darker path, and couldn't save the civilizations of their birth.<br /> <br /> A mantle isn't simply something that changes from one culture to the next, however. Aphrodite is Venus in Rome, sure, but there's also Venus Castina, who is a different aspect of Venus altogether. There are versions of Diana that emphasize different qualities. In Greece, there were different 'faces' for Hermes, Demeter, and Dionysus depending on what Mystery Cult you were dealing with.<br /> <br /> I hope that helped explain how mantles might work, I worry that it wasn't much more clear than the kickstarter blurb.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=990889#post990889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something like that.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm greedy - I want all the mantles. I kind of halfway suspect this is how we'll get Hathor and Sekhmet into the game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I really really hope not, thankfully given the response from Neall I don't think they'll foist Hathor and Sekhmet off as being 'simply mantles' of existent gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","user":"Solana","date":". 10-21-2016, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T05:55:45-07:00","id":990923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=990918#post990918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really really hope not, thankfully given the response from Neall I don't think they'll foist Hathor and Sekhmet off as being 'simply mantles' of existent gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should be clear that my two sentences were two separate things. I am not quite as optimistic, hence my suspicion about Hathor and Sekhmet.<br /> <br /> Would rather they just got to be in with the other Egyptian deities, though. And hopefully that's what will happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T13:16:55-07:00","id":991081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=990886#post990886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry guys, but i didn't understand well what mantle is:<br /> <br /> The &quot;mantle&quot; a god can wear is the other face of the god? maybe in another culture?<br /> <br /> For example: Mithra is a god in Yazata Pantheon, in Deva And he's loved even by Roman. All this face of the same god are different mantle?<br /> <br /> Hades - Pluto<br /> Venus - Aphrodite<br /> <br /> When a god is shared between pantheons, he's changing the mantle...? right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes, but not always. Ares/Mars has two very distinct mantles depending on whether he's in a Greek or Roman context. Yama belongs to several pantheons, but doesn't seem to have different mantles for them.<br /> <br /> In addition, some Gods have multiple mantles within the same pantheon. The Orisha concept of &quot;caminos&quot; is a good example of this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","user":"Robert Vance","date":". 10-21-2016, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T13:28:43-07:00","id":991086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=991081#post991081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes, but not always. Ares/Mars has two very distinct mantles depending on whether he's in a Greek or Roman context. Yama belongs to several pantheons, but doesn't seem to have different mantles for them.<br /> <br /> In addition, some Gods have multiple mantles within the same pantheon. The Orisha concept of &quot;caminos&quot; is a good example of this.</div> </div> </div> </div>A solar deity like Ra who changes his moods depending where the sun is, is aclso changinc mantles?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T13:34:04-07:00","id":991089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=991086#post991086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A solar deity like Ra who changes his moods depending where the sun is, is aclso changinc mantles?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that makes sense for Re, but I'm not a Kemetic expert.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T13:45:54-07:00","id":991095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=991089#post991089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that makes sense for Re, but I'm not a Kemetic expert.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then could you tell me. What's the difference between a god simply changing his mind and personality with the time and a god changing his mantle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T13:56:25-07:00","id":991097,"title":"","content":"Perhaps different Mantles of Aphrodite reflect different Greek concepts of love.<br /> <br /> Aphrodite Urania of course rules over heavenly Agape.<br /> <br /> Aphrodite Pandemos, her most well known &quot;default&quot; Mantle rules over earthly sexual Erotes.<br /> <br /> Venus, mother of Aeneus, mother of Divius Julius, mother of Rome, rules over familial Storge.<br /> <br /> <br /> Not sure on Phillia...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T14:02:31-07:00","id":991098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=991095#post991095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then could you tell me. What's the difference between a god simply changing his mind and personality with the time and a god changing his mantle?</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that a Mantle is, basically, another God.<br /> <br /> So a God with multiple mantles is multiple gods rolled up in one.<br /> <br /> Something that Gods can do in Scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T14:03:31-07:00","id":991099,"title":"","content":"I wonder if we might see Mars Nodens, patron of wounded veterans and keeper of the hounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T14:16:51-07:00","id":991105,"title":"","content":"I can only imagine that the Mantles guide will also go into more detail on like, Brigid and the Morrigan having three different aspects/faces.<br /> <br /> And NOW I'm imagining three Scion siblings, with each one a Scion of a different mantle of Brigid. Fun times!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T14:49:39-07:00","id":991133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=991095#post991095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then could you tell me. What's the difference between a god simply changing his mind and personality with the time and a god changing his mantle?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ares didn't become Mars because he calmed down. He became Mars when the Romans saw that he was now this calmer, imperial god of war, and began worshipping him as such, defining the new Mantle within Fate. A God changing his mind is much less dramatic than changing between their Mantles\u2014Mars can still go back to being Ares if he feels like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T14:58:03-07:00","id":991140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=991095#post991095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then could you tell me. What's the difference between a god simply changing his mind and personality with the time and a god changing his mantle?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the difference between Zeus as arbiter of justice (see King Lycaon myths) and Zeus as incorrigible sex addict in another myth. They're both just facets of his personality. <br /> <br /> A mantle would be Kinich Ahau, Mayan god of the sun, becoming the Jaguar god of terrestrial fire upon entering the Underworld. A lot of Mayan gods have 'alternate identities' when day turns to night, and the world passes into (or near) the underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T15:08:50-07:00","id":991145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=991133#post991133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ares didn't become Mars because he calmed down. He became Mars when the Romans saw that he was now this calmer, imperial god of war, and began worshipping him as such, defining the new Mantle within Fate. A God changing his mind is much less dramatic than changing between their Mantles\u2014Mars can still go back to being Ares if he feels like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ares became Mars when the Romans were as bloody and awful as him <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T15:48:09-07:00","id":991154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=991133#post991133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ares didn't become Mars because he calmed down. He became Mars when the Romans saw that he was now this calmer, imperial god of war, and began worshipping him as such, defining the new Mantle within Fate. A God changing his mind is much less dramatic than changing between their Mantles\u2014Mars can still go back to being Ares if he feels like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah,that's nice. Thanks Robert","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T16:11:13-07:00","id":991162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=991097#post991097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps different Mantles of Aphrodite reflect different Greek concepts of love.<br /> <br /> Aphrodite Urania of course rules over heavenly Agape.<br /> <br /> Aphrodite Pandemos, her most well known &amp;quot;default&amp;quot; Mantle rules over earthly sexual Erotes.<br /> <br /> Venus, mother of Aeneus, mother of Divius Julius, mother of Rome, rules over familial Storge.<br /> <br /> <br /> Not sure on Phillia...</div> </div> </div> </div>Other Aphrodites, Cyrian Goddess of Lesbians and Areia a war Goddess to the Spartans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T16:39:03-07:00","id":991172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_names_of_Freyja\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ec/Freyja_and_the_Necklace_by_James_Doyle_Penrose%2C_1890.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_names_of_Freyja\" target=\"_blank\"> Freyja - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_names_of_Freyja\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_names_of_Freyja </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Some ideas for Freyja.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T17:05:09-07:00","id":991181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bastet\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Bastet.svg/960px-Bastet.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bastet\" target=\"_blank\"> Bastet - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bastet\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bastet </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Mantles for Bastet, could be Mut, Wadjet, Sekhmet, Nekhbet.<br /> <br /> Mut is the key here because she became connected to both Wadjet-Bast and Sekhmet-Nekhbet, so I feel like if Bastet and Sekhmet are going to be depicted as the same Goddess, then then Mut is the connection they really need for it to work. Just my opinion.<br /> <br /> And some where their should be a reference to her title the perfumed protector.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T19:28:49-07:00","id":991224,"title":"","content":"King Yama is literally too busy to make mantles. He's been saying he'd get to it eventually ever since the Buddha showed up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T20:33:43-07:00","id":991240,"title":"","content":"Perhaps a bit obvious, but I didn't catch it mentioned: I can think of 9 (or 10 if you want to put Buddha in there, but I'd rather he be something else) famous Mantles of Vishnu off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> Where you draw the line between Mantle and separate goddesses with... Shiva's wife (Durga, Parvati, Kali...) is incredibly complicated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T20:39:21-07:00","id":991246,"title":"","content":"I wonder if a Mantle can Incarnate while the God still lives in another form... like if Loki the murderer of Baldr bent on destruction of the Aesir were currently bound with a snake dripping poison on his face, could Loki the trickster adventurer incarnate theirself in the World and potentially do good?<br /> <br /> Or more traditional case: could a Mantle of a Deva Incarnate itself as an PC Avatar even while the greater Deva still lived?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T21:21:39-07:00","id":991267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=991246#post991246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if a Mantle can Incarnate while the God still lives in another form... like if Loki the murderer of Baldr bent on destruction of the Aesir were currently bound with a snake dripping poison on his face, could Loki the trickster adventurer incarnate theirself in the World and potentially do good?<br /> <br /> Or more traditional case: could a Mantle of a Deva Incarnate itself as an PC Avatar even while the greater Deva still lived?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to wonder if death-and-rebirth deities have gone through that myth in the past, or if that myth is always a constant and somehow always happening in a sort of weird Schrodinger situation. Because if the latter, I imagine Azar/Osiris has many, many more Incarnate Scions than everyone else among the Netjer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T23:23:33-07:00","id":991300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=991099#post991099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if we might see Mars Nodens, patron of wounded veterans and keeper of the hounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nodens was a legit god, though. A god who was syncretised with Mars by the Romans when they took over Britain, but still his own god. Making him just a mantle of Mars/Ares would be incredibly stupid and I hope that they don't do anything like that.<br /> <br /> I'd rather see him as his own, unique god but if they did have to make him a mantle I'd rather it be of Nuada or something, not fucking Mars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12300,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","user":"Crying","date":". 10-24-2016, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T05:32:13-07:00","id":991350,"title":"","content":"Mantles might best be put as 'when we're pretty sure one god has multiple distinct identities, and those identities act very differently'. A good example might be the Doctor of <i>Doctor Who</i> - each Doctor has their own individual identity, their own personality and idiosyncracies, but they're all recognisable as &quot;the Doctor&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T10:36:05-07:00","id":991437,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the proper way to do Hathor/Sekhmet would be as one goddess with two wildly different mantles. Most deities don't go through quite that dramatic a shift from one mantle to another, but I like the idea of those two being the concept taken to its extreme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9296-zeldafan42","name":"Zeldafan42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9296_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T10:36:40-07:00","id":991438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=991097#post991097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps different Mantles of Aphrodite reflect different Greek concepts of love.<br /> <br /> Aphrodite Urania of course rules over heavenly Agape.<br /> <br /> Aphrodite Pandemos, her most well known &quot;default&quot; Mantle rules over earthly sexual Erotes.<br /> <br /> Venus, mother of Aeneus, mother of Divius Julius, mother of Rome, rules over familial Storge.<br /> <br /> <br /> Not sure on Phillia...</div> </div> </div> </div>How about Aphrodite Philomeides, Laughter-Loving?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5530,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","user":"Xanthias","date":". 10-22-2016, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T10:41:28-07:00","id":991441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeldafan42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=991437#post991437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the proper way to do Hathor/Sekhmet would be as one goddess with two wildly different mantles. Most deities don't go through quite that dramatic a shift from one mantle to another, but I like the idea of those two being the concept taken to its extreme.</div> </div> </div> </div> You mean Isis/Hathor, Sekhmet got merged with Bastet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T10:54:46-07:00","id":991453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=991441#post991441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean Isis/Hathor, Sekhmet got merged with Bastet.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I mean that the right way to do Hathor and Sekhmet is to forget this idea of merging Hathor with Isis and Sekhmet with Bast, and instead use the familiar myth of bloodthirsty Sekhmet being placated with booze to become nurturing Hathor, and use the two of them to demonstrate the extreme end of mantles, an example of a deity that changes not just their personality with their mantle, but an entire change in purviews and maybe callings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9296-zeldafan42","name":"Zeldafan42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9296_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T11:50:17-07:00","id":991465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeldafan42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=991453#post991453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I mean that the right way to do Hathor and Sekhmet is to forget this idea of merging Hathor with Isis and Sekhmet with Bast, and instead use the familiar myth of bloodthirsty Sekhmet being placated with booze to become nurturing Hathor, and use the two of them to demonstrate the extreme end of mantles, an example of a deity that changes not just their personality with their mantle, but an entire change in purviews and maybe callings.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not sure why everyone is going with the interpretation that Sekhmet is now some great nurturer, the curse's terms were that she could now only break 'hearts' which is far from a nurturing figure. I support her being her own goddess specifically because her personality is so contrary to Hathor, and even her association with the purview of Love is different. The difference is one goddess singing 'Love is a Battlefield' and another singing 'Love Will Find a Way'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T12:04:22-07:00","id":991469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=991441#post991441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean Isis/Hathor, Sekhmet got merged with Bastet.</div> </div> </div> </div>A choice I hope they'll change their minds on after the massive fan outcry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T12:20:47-07:00","id":991477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=990886#post990886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry guys, but i didn't understand well what mantle is:<br /> <br /> The &amp;quot;mantle&amp;quot; a god can wear is the other face of the god? maybe in another culture? <br /> <br /> For example: Mithra is a god in Yazata Pantheon, in Deva And he's loved even by Roman. All this face of the same god are different mantle? <br /> <br /> Hades - Pluto <br /> Venus - Aphrodite<br /> <br /> When a god is shared between pantheons, he's changing the mantle...? right?</div> </div> </div> </div> Imagine a God as someone with multiple personalities disorder, except each personality comes with a physical and spiritual transformation, and in some cases its possible for said personalities to create incarnations, seperate weaker bodies. <br /> <br /> I believe they are created via fatebinding.<br /> <br /> So God A is worshipped by three very different groups. Group A is familiar with God A normal original personality/identity, and as worships accordingly.<br /> <br /> Group B's High Priest, well he likes to get creative so he makes shit up while you weren't paying attention, and he gets your worshippers to buy into it, say that your true form is a red furred monkey with magical boobs growing out of your forehead, call Abba.<br /> <br /> Eventually Fate takes notice and you devoloped a servile secondary personality called Abba, aka a mantle.<br /> <br /> Group C is lead by a Priestess who realizes her people really need a rain god, but that's not really you at all. So she creatively she embellishes and the next thing you know you have a Mantle of being a generous rain god.<br /> <br /> Group C sees you get drunk, while sniffing coke off a sex workers ass one time while on The World, and they start to see you as a God of Booze, Sex Workers, and Coke, and eventually that leads to some myths, so Fate makes another Mantle for you.<br /> <br /> Another way to look at it, each Mantle is an Acting Role, with Supernatural Customes and SFX, and while in the role you ARE role, but you can take off the role later or switch between the roles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T12:27:24-07:00","id":991482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=991469#post991469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A choice I hope they'll change their minds on after the massive fan outcry.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm okay with Bastet/Sekhmet being Mantles of the same Cat deity, if they do it right and bring in Mut, she's the connection between the two. In fact maybe Sekhmet, Bastet, Wadjet, Nekhbet should all be Mantles for Mut, all have been linked to Mut.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T12:29:34-07:00","id":991484,"title":"","content":"This is a little off-topic but related. When they introduced the stretch goal related to mantles, the first thing that occured to me is how neat it would be for a PC to have to interact with a different mantle of their parent. Someone up the thread used the example of the Doctor from Doctor Who as an example of what a mantle is.. It would be neat to just follow that idea to its logical conclusion.<br /> <br /> &quot;You're not my mother!&quot;<br /> &quot;Well dear, that's a little complicated...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1789-quinarch","name":"Quinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1789_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T12:31:05-07:00","id":991485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=991482#post991482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm okay with Bastet/Sekhmet being Mantles of the same Cat deity, if they do it right and bring in Mut, she's the connection between the two. In fact maybe Sekhmet, Bastet, Wadjet, Nekhbet should all be Mantles for Mut, all have been linked to Mut.</div> </div> </div> </div>Playing a Scion of Nekhbet would be awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T15:12:18-07:00","id":991551,"title":"","content":"I might make that suggestion in its own thread, see if people like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T16:08:24-07:00","id":991576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=991465#post991465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm not sure why everyone is going with the interpretation that Sekhmet is now some great nurturer, the curse's terms were that she could now only break 'hearts' which is far from a nurturing figure. I support her being her own goddess specifically because her personality is so contrary to Hathor, and even her association with the purview of Love is different. The difference is one goddess singing 'Love is a Battlefield' and another singing 'Love Will Find a Way'</div> </div> </div> </div>But there's literally a myth about how they're the same goddess based on how bloodthirsty vs drunk she is at the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T16:23:12-07:00","id":991583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=991576#post991576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there's literally a myth about how they're the same goddess based on how bloodthirsty vs drunk she is at the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a version of the myth where she was Hathor and is transformed into Sekhmet by Ra in order to do a job, but it is not 'the myth' of how Sekhmet was sent by Ra to do that. There are other versions of that Myth where the two are not conflated, and they otherwise have nothing to do with each other in temperament even after the gods make it so she can no longer engage in wanton slaughter. Aside from that myth, she had her own festivals, priestesses, and role in Egyptian society.<br /> <br /> So I suppose a better way of communicating it, is that I'm not sure why people would want to conflate Sekhmet with Hathor, except because one interpretation of the myth in the The Book of the Heavenly Cow says they're the same. For my purposes, that's not a valid enough reason to run with them being the same person. Sekhmet has children of her own that are not associated with Hathor, Hathor has likewise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","user":"Solana","date":". 10-22-2016, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T16:28:28-07:00","id":991588,"title":"","content":"I don't really see any good reason to argue for the game about gods having one <i>less</i> god in it. Can you smash them together? Sure, but then instead of a mother cow goddess of women and gemstones <i>and</i> a bloodthirsty lion goddess who nearly exterminated humanity, you get a weird cow-lion who loves and slaughters the human race depending on her mood and blood alcohol level.. and I can tell you, that third option is how precisely none of the Egyptian viewed her.<br /> <br /> Much in the same way that I object to the Netjer preview draft giving us not Bast and Sekhmet, but instead a wretched middle option that's more like the scary homeless person you try to avoid than either of these deities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 10-22-2016, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T17:00:42-07:00","id":991602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=991588#post991588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really see any good reason to argue for the game about gods having one <i>less</i> god in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once you assume that position though, Re doesn't get to do half his myths because Atum did that, or Khepri did that, or Heru-the-Elder, etc etc. Egyptian myth is entirely shaped by the combining and conflating of deities. It's just the question of which conflations. I promise the version of Egyptian Myth any given person on this thread prefers as the &quot;most accurate&quot; version was built on divine conflations of earlier myths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T17:01:10-07:00","id":991603,"title":"","content":"Ok, I'm going to clarify my early post with the knowledge that Egyptian mythology is not my strong point. I only suggested the Hathor/Sekhmet merger because I've heard that myth from several sources, and assumed the myth that connects them must be a common myth because of that. If the two of them aren't actually that commonly conflated together, then I suppose we're probably better off just leaving them separate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9296-zeldafan42","name":"Zeldafan42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9296_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T17:11:55-07:00","id":991609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeldafan42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=991603#post991603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I'm going to clarify my early post with the knowledge that Egyptian mythology is not my strong point. I only suggested the Hathor/Sekhmet merger because I've heard that myth from several sources, and assumed the myth that connects them must be a common myth because of that. If the two of them aren't actually that commonly conflated together, then I suppose we're probably better off just leaving them separate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I think the Hathor/Sekhmet conflation is the most interesting route to go with them as a twin aspected goddess of creation and destruction is inherently cool, and serves to make her more distinct from more guardian, less destructive, non-Creation-Goddess Bastet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T17:24:26-07:00","id":991614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=991609#post991609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I think the Hathor/Sekhmet conflation is the most interesting route to go with them as a twin aspected goddess of creation and destruction is inherently cool, and serves to make her more distinct from more guardian, less destructive, non-Creation-Goddess Bastet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine that most mantles are subtle changes, that at best alter one or two purviews and maybe a calling.<br /> <br /> The main thing I liked about the idea of using the myth that combines Hathor and Sekhmet into a singular entity is that not only is it well known, but it would give us a deity that takes mantles to their logical extreme, where the two mantles are so dramatically different that they probably completely change the purviews and callings associated with the two sides. Yeah, it'd probably be easier to just make them separate deities, but this way you could also model an example of a mantle that creates an extreme shift in a deity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9296-zeldafan42","name":"Zeldafan42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9296_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T19:11:31-07:00","id":991657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeldafan42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=991603#post991603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I'm going to clarify my early post with the knowledge that Egyptian mythology is not my strong point. I only suggested the Hathor/Sekhmet merger because I've heard that myth from several sources, and assumed the myth that connects them must be a common myth because of that. If the two of them aren't actually that commonly conflated together, then I suppose we're probably better off just leaving them separate.</div> </div> </div> </div>The myth is brought up often because the book itself was a pretty big find, but seeing it in several places on the internet does not mean that the myth as it's recorded in the book is recorded that way in many places back when it was relevant. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeldafan42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=991614#post991614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I imagine that most mantles are subtle changes, that at best alter one or two purviews and maybe a calling.<br /> <br /> The main thing I liked about the idea of using the myth that combines Hathor and Sekhmet into a singular entity is that not only is it well known, but it would give us a deity that takes mantles to their logical extreme, where the two mantles are so dramatically different that they probably completely change the purviews and callings associated with the two sides. Yeah, it'd probably be easier to just make them separate deities, but this way you could also model an example of a mantle that creates an extreme shift in a deity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think stretching the Mantle system until it should break does the definition any favors. If you take two goddesses who are distinct from one another, and then use a myth as an excuse to push them together, what you will get is one goddess with a mantle that is contrary to her in every way. Sekhmet has different purviews from Hathor, different Callings from Hathor, she has her own festivals, priestesses, sacred days, etc. She has her own Scions in the mythology, which have nothing to do with Hathor. In this context the notion of a mantle would have literally no meaning at all because for all intents and purposes, Hathor and her mantle of Sekhmet are completely different gods. You could say that Sekhmet is a mantle of her, or that Sekhmet is a goddess in her own right, but the practical result would be exactly the same either way. <br /> <br /> So why do it? The only way I can think of to distinguish it is to truly conflate the gods into one being, which would be the mythological equivalent of Dr. Hathor and Ms. Sekhmet. At least the Morrigan in all of her aspects draws from a common theme, Brigid likewise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=991609#post991609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> Oh, I think the Hathor/Sekhmet conflation is the most interesting route to go with them as a twin aspected goddess of creation and destruction is inherently cool, and serves to make her more distinct from more guardian, less destructive, non-Creation-Goddess Bastet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the irony is that you just said they are pretty distinct from each other already. Bastet is a guardian deity who isn't destructive, isn't tied to the royal family, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T20:23:26-07:00","id":991684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=991657#post991657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the irony is that you just said they are pretty distinct from each other already. Bastet is a guardian deity who isn't destructive, isn't tied to the royal family, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the case very late - but early on you've got effectively identical goddesses of war in lower (Bastet) and upper (Sekhmet) Egypt. It is completely valid with that in mind to treat Bastet's guardian behavior relative to Sekhmet's destructiveness the same way the game treats the differences between murderous Ares and disciplined Mars.<br /> <br /> Sekhmet-Hathor as goddess of creation &amp; destruction is the strongest alternative to that IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T22:50:09-07:00","id":991735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990848-what-mantles-would-you-like-to-see?p=991684#post991684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's the case very late - but early on you've got effectively identical goddesses of war in lower (Bastet) and upper (Sekhmet) Egypt. It is completely valid with that in mind to treat Bastet's guardian behavior relative to Sekhmet's destructiveness the same way the game treats the differences between murderous Ares and disciplined Mars.<br /> <br /> Sekhmet-Hathor as goddess of creation &amp; destruction is the strongest alternative to that IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bastet's status as a goddess of war was downplayed considerably with the unification of Upper and Lower Egypt. She became more of a apotropaic goddess to Sekhmet's flat-out war goddess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}